  "assumptions": [
    "Idealized model: small swings, period T = 2π√(L/g) with g = 9.81 m/s² (exact in the model, close for real swings under about 15°).",
    "The string is light and doesn't stretch; the bob is treated as a point at the string's end.",
    "No air resistance or friction, so the swing never dies down; the swing starts at a fixed 12° angle.",
    "The swing angle is computed from the clock time, so changing the length jumps the bob to the new swing's position at that moment; the timeline loop also restarts the swing every 60 s.",
    "Large-angle lengthening of the period and damping are not shown."
  ],
  "program": {
    "source": "export function evaluate({ inputs, time }) {\n  const L = inputs.length;\n  const T = 2 * Math.PI * Math.sqrt(L / 9.81);\n  const th = (12 * Math.PI / 180) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * time / T);\n  return {\n    nodes: {\n      arm: { quaternion: [0, 0, Math.sin(th / 2), Math.cos(th / 2)] },\n      str: { position: [0, -L / 2, 0], scale: [1, L, 1] },\n      bobN: { position: [0, -L, 0] }\n    },\n    readouts: { period: T, len: L }\n  };\n}\n"
  }
